<p>I'm a very lenient canon-enforcer. I feel weird when I downvote for concept. I feel extra weird when I act like a pedant about a particular canonical element someone introduces and actually bother to comment about it, but I am fundamentally opposed to this.</p>
<p>I am so tired of pataphysics. This is the article that's making me admit that. I don't even have the words for it. It's a wave of exhausting over-meta that is going to tire the site of meta content in general <em>very quickly</em> because it takes it so damn hard and makes it so <em>overt.</em> We could have stuck with the existence of the Multi-U Department, the implications of Swann's Proposal, and <a href="/metafiction">Timeline R-zayin-H-517/6.</a> That was enough. I respect any author's approach to meta, as its very subjective, but this pataphysics business is almost <em>objectively</em> going to burn up all the site's meta juice. Give it a few months; pataphysics is too much of a gimmick to produce unique content after a certain period, I guarantee it.</p>
<p>There ain't shit I can do about it other than be annoyed, and the upvotes prove that I'm in the minority, but it's not something I can let myself be quiet about.</p>

