			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3901161">
									

<p>I'll straight up admit I'm not super into the pataphysics trend that has swept through some corners on the wiki, however, I'd like to think that an article that was executed well enough could still wring a +1 out of me. This is not that article I'm afraid.</p>
<p>Not only do you basically serve us the entire wiki as a kind of bizarro version of itself in this SCP, the handling of the authorship in the O5 discussion at the end just kills the piece for me, as it's not only rather hamhanded but also dull exposition on how this brand of pataphysics works.</p>
<p>Even if the above were not the case, in the end, the whole affair just rings far to close to Swann's Proposal for my liking.</p>
<p>Perhaps if this was more subtle about how it does business things would be different, but then again would that not just be Swann's proposal again?</p>
